    "description": "Top-down schematic of the inner solar system. Six planet circles ride orbital ellipses centered on the Sun. Each carries a SMIL rotate-loop with periodMs scaled by its real orbital year — Mercury whips around once per ~1.9s, Saturn drifts once per ~3m55s. Asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter. Saturn's rings co-rotate with the planet. What NASA Eyes does in 3D, Glyph does as a flat orrery.",
